  "equipment_type": "VRF BACnet IP gateway",
  "applies_to": "Fujitsu General Airstage V-II / J-II / VR-II VRF indoor and outdoor units on the VRF network.",
  "summary": "The UTY-VBGX connects a Fujitsu Airstage VRF network to BACnet IP and creates a fixed set of objects for every indoor and outdoor unit it finds, plus gateway-wide batch commands. Object names and instances are built from the refrigerant system and unit addresses, so the instance number tells you which unit a point belongs to. Device name, instance and port are set with the Fujitsu configuration tool.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet IP"
  ],
  "firmware": null,
  "default_device_instance": 144000,
  "notes": [
    "Indoor unit instances are TTrruu: TT = point code (10-17), rr = refrigerant system address (00-99), uu = indoor unit address (00-63). Instances here use rr=01, uu=01 (e.g. 100101).",
    "Outdoor unit instances are 30rruu-32rruu with uu = outdoor unit address (0-3). Gateway and batch objects use fixed low instances (0-2).",
    "The detailed object pages give different OU instances (ForcedOff_Setting 30rruu, CapacitySave_Status 32rruu, CapacitySave_Setting 33rruu) than the summary table used here; verify on site.",
    "The object table lists the device as 144000; the configuration tool section says the default Device Instance is 144. Each gateway needs a unique value.",
    "Outputs keep Priority_Array slots 1-15 empty and mirror Present_Value in slot 16; State_Text must be read one array index at a time.",
    "Error code and RC prohibition state texts are long lookup tables in the manual and are not reproduced here."
  ],
